        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "**Maximum credits you can carry this semester:** 40 credits (the absolute cap for any semester).\n\n**Logistical conflict on Mondays:** The AI‑branch Semester 4 lab courses (e.g., *Data Structure Lab* AIC2912 and *Electronics Laboratory* ELA2902) are scheduled from 02:00 PM to 04:30 PM, which exactly overlaps the two labs you already have in your Computer Engineering timetable (Digital Design & Simulation Lab COC2922 and Electronics Laboratory ELA2902). Registering any additional Monday‑afternoon lab will create a time‑slot clash, making it impossible to attend both sessions."
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "If the AI course I want to take is a 'Programme Core' (PC), how many credits does it typically carry, and would adding it put me over the 40-credit limit?"
      },
      {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "**Typical credit value for a Programme‑Core (PC) AI course:** 4 credits (most PC courses in the AI programme are 4‑credit theory courses; a few are 2‑ or 3‑credit labs, but the standard is 4 credits).\n\n**Effect on the 40‑credit semester cap:** Adding a 4‑credit PC course will keep you within the 40‑credit limit **provided your current registered load is 36 credits or fewer**. If you are already carrying 37 credits or more, the extra 4 credits would push you past the hard‑cap and registration would be rejected."
      }
